3. The vending machine should be able to dispense the selected product if enough money has been inserted.
4. If the selected product costs more than the amount inserted, the vending machine should display a message asking for more money.
5. If the vending machine does not have enough change to return to the customer, it should display an error message and refund all money inserted.
6. The vending machine should have an option to display the total amount of money inserted so far.
7. The vending machine should have an option to cancel the transaction and receive a refund of all money inserted.

